  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bell Textron has $2.1B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Bell Textron has received 891 awards so far this fiscal year and the average award size is $2.3M. Bell Textron obligations are up 36.8% year over year. The Department of Defense accounts for the vast majority of Bell Textron obligations with $2B so far in FY2026. Aircraft Manufacturing is Bell Textron's largest market at $1.8B, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $249M. The FY2026 totals are partial because the period covers the fiscal year to date, and award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How much has Bell Textron received in obligations this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Bell Textron has $2.1B in obligations for FY2026 to date. Bell Textron has 891 awards and an average award size of $2.3M. Bell Textron obligations are up 36.8% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers and what markets does Bell Textron serve?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $2B to Bell Textron in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Interior obligated $53.2M, the Department of Justice obligated $717K, the Department of Transportation obligated $135K, and the Department of Energy obligated $58.5K. Aircraft Manufacturing is Bell Textron's largest market at $1.8B, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $249M and Scale and Balance Manufacturing at $2M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
